From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: preserve decoder visible crop across CAPTURE S_FMT

iris_vdec_s_fmt() overwrote inst->crop with the CAPTURE buffer dimensions on
S_FMT(CAPTURE). Because v4l2_codec2 calls G_FMT, S_FMT, and
G_SELECTION(V4L2_SEL_TGT_COMPOSE) after receiving V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE,
resetting inst->crop clobbered the stream's visible crop rectangle reported by
the firmware in HFI_EVENT_DATA_SEQUENCE_CHANGED (e.g. reporting 1920x1088
instead of 1920x1080 for 1080p H.264).

Preserve inst->crop across S_FMT(CAPTURE), as it is initialized on
S_FMT(OUTPUT) and updated by firmware sequence-changed events.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
index b638d58c3..55cfd2be0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
@@ -299,11 +299,6 @@ int iris_vdec_s_fmt(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_format *f)
 		fmt->fmt.pix_mp.plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = iris_get_buffer_size(inst, BUF_OUTPUT);
 		inst->buffers[BUF_OUTPUT].min_count = iris_vpu_buf_count(inst, BUF_OUTPUT);
 		inst->buffers[BUF_OUTPUT].size = fmt->fmt.pix_mp.plane_fmt[0].sizeimage;
-
-		inst->crop.top = 0;
-		inst->crop.left = 0;
-		inst->crop.width = f->fmt.pix_mp.width;
-		inst->crop.height = f->fmt.pix_mp.height;
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
